===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*tanþs}} (by loss of the ''n'' and the resulting [[w:compensatory lengthening|compensatory lengthening]] of the vowel), from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*h₃dónts|t=tooth}}. Cognates with {{cog|ofs|tōth}}, {{cog|osx|tand}}, {{cog|nl|tand}}, {{cog|goh|zan}}, {{m|goh|zand}} ({{cog|de|Zahn}}), {{cog|non|tǫnn}} ({{cog|sv|tand}}), {{cog|got|𐍄𐌿𐌽𐌸𐌿𐍃}}; and with {{cog|sa|दन्त}} ({{cog|hi|दांत}}), {{cog|grc|ὀδών}}, {{cog|la|dens}} ({{cog|fr|dent}}), {{cog|sga|dét}}, {{cog|lt|dantìs}}.

